    "notes": "1. The 'total_revenue' field is constructed from the sum of 'Automotive' and 'GM Financial' revenue lines, which are explicitly detailed in the statement. The 'Total net sales and revenue' line is also included as it represents the consolidated total. 2. The 'total_operating_cost' field is constructed from the sum of 'Automotive and other cost of sales', 'GM Financial interest, operating and other expenses', and 'Automotive and other selling, general and administrative expense'. The 'Total costs and expenses' line is also included as the consolidated total. 3. The 'net_income' field is constructed from the 'Net income (loss)' line, adjusted for 'Net loss (income) attributable to noncontrolling interests' to arrive at 'Net income (loss) attributable to stockholders', which is the final consolidated net income figure. The sign for the noncontrolling interest adjustment is reversed per rule 13, as it is an addition to income for the parent company. 4. 'Taxes' is directly mapped from 'Income tax expense (benefit)'. 5. 'Interest_expenses' is directly mapped from 'Automotive interest expense'. GM Financial's interest expense is included within its operating costs and is therefore part of 'total_operating_cost'. 6. All values are in millions (scale: 1E6). 7. The supplementary tables provide detailed breakdowns but were not required for the construction of the core income statement fields as per the schema.",
